  "term": "fetal alcohol syndrome",
  "definition": "Fetal alcohol syndrome is a disorder in a baby or child caused by alcohol exposure during pregnancy. It can involve low birth weight, unusual facial features, small head size, poor growth, developmental and organ problems, intellectual difficulties, poor motor coordination, and behavior problems.",
